  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Periodic showers through tonight, then some lake \neffect rain showers Monday. \n\nPrefrontal trough moving through the region this afternoon. A \nweakening band of showers associated with this feature will pass \nacross western New York early this afternoon, and then any \nremaining shower activity will reach central New York by mid \nafternoon.\n\nA potent shortwave tracking across James Bay will send a sharp cold \nfront through the eastern Great Lakes tonight. With the front expect \nsome additional showers to work through the region overnight.\n\nA cooler airmass will settle in behind the front with 850 mb \ntemperatures dropping just below zero C (-1C to -3C) by Monday \nevening. Given the chilly airmass aloft moving across the warm lake \nwaters and some limited remaining shallow moisture, it is likely\nwe will see some lake induced clouds and even a few lake induced\nrain showers as the trough axis pivots through the region.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Below average temperatures expected Monday, \nwidespread frost likely Monday night. \n\nThe incoming cooler airmass will bring an early fall chill in the \nair Monday, with afternoon highs only expected in the upper 40s\nto 50s. It will also be quite breezy Monday, with winds gusting\nup to 30 to 35 mph, making it feel even cooler. Surface high \npressure moving nearly overhead Monday night will allow \ntemperatures to bottom out in the 30s, with some upper 20s \npossible in the coldest inland locations. A widespread frost \nlooks likely during this period.",
